    "updated_at": "2024-06-20T07:04:39Z",
    "body": "> I wish this had a clearer name given these semantics.\r\n\r\nI had these same regrets at first. However I think I remember the reasoning now. Basically, the `hashchange` event only fires for fragment navigations; it doesn't actually fire for all hash changes. So to web developers, the API name for \"fragment navigation\" is \"hash change\", and there is no API concept for \"`location.hash` has changed\".\r\n\r\nIn other words, this is a consistency-vs.-goodness tradeoff where we chose consistency. Maybe we could've debated a bit more at the time, especially in the context of the navigation API trying to be the new replacement so you don't have to think about old APIs like `hashchange`. But, oh well.",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
